{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/792267-ananasi-too-special-snowflake","id":792267,"title":"Ananasi: Too Special Snowflake?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-24T11:24:16-08:00","id":792267,"title":"Ananasi: Too Special Snowflake?","content":"Not trying to troll or start a war, just looking for anyone to enlighten me as to the whys and wherefores of the Spider people, and shift away from the my view that they are too special snowflake.<br /> <br /> After reading the Ananasi tribe book again, i am left with the fact that, even accounting for being written from their POV and biased as a result, the Ananasi reek to me of &quot;Secretly Awesome Guys Who Are Totes Wiser, Smarter and Better Than You.&quot;<br /> <br /> They were created by the Spider Queen who is the Weavers sister, they know the truth about everything and only they can save the world since all the other Fera are utterly irrelevant.<br /> <br /> I'd like people to provide counter arguments to my conclusion that they are just more trouble than they are worth as a splat, and that they can have a place to play in the setting besides being the Shadow Stues of the CWoD.<br /> <br /> Any takers please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1919,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","user":"muadib","date":". 12-24-2015, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T11:28:33-08:00","id":792269,"title":"","content":"Have you ever read the Kitsune Corebook? That stuff is even worse. Don't get me wrong, I love White Wolf, but their books are more biased than a political debate in North Korea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T12:41:59-08:00","id":792310,"title":"","content":"Ok in fairness the 2nd Appendix is written OOC. And is decent at putting the lie to a large portion of the Ananasi writ. But this renforces my problem. As described the Spiders are a sociopathic cult dedicated to their Queen. Empathy and Compassion are Flaws that give you pts.<br /> <br /> Has anyone run a game with a werespider in it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1919-muadib","name":"muadib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T16:52:14-08:00","id":792433,"title":"","content":"I did, actually. She was.. different to say the least. The general promise was that the tribes decided to join up against the constant threat of the Wyrm (and yeah, they tried to forgive the werewolves for the whole Killing Everybody thing) and so, of course, an Ananasi joined, too. She and the Tengu I played got along pretty well, considering that she hid her sociopathic nature very well. The only thing that really got between them was the fact that he lied to her about Tengu Blood being highly toxic and her... well lets just say he didn't sleep all that well for a while. <br /> <br /> From what I gathered, yes, Ananasi can be a pain to play with. But if you have a good GM like I had, it evens out a little. They caught well on Ananasi being relatively few and thus not as well-informed and known as other tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-24T18:42:50-08:00","id":792469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>muadib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/792267-ananasi-too-special-snowflake#post792267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the Ananasi tribe book again, i am left with the fact that, even accounting for being written from their POV and biased as a result, the Ananasi reek to me of &quot;Secretly Awesome Guys Who Are Totes Wiser, Smarter and Better Than You.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Now read all the other Splat books. They claim the same stuff (arguably Bastet is probably still the worst in the special snowflake department). In their own books they are all special and they are the only ones that really &quot;Get&quot; the universe. It's normal stuff. They're no less snowflaky then any of th other factions.<br /> <br /> The Ananasi do have a slightly different play style from the other shifters, but they excel at underhanded and subtle manipulations, something the other shifters usually don't deal with. They're also not the best team players, but neither are the Kitsune, Bastet, Nuwisha, Gurahl or the Corax... so...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T02:25:50-08:00","id":792680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/792267-ananasi-too-special-snowflake?p=792469#post792469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now read all the other Splat books. They claim the same stuff (arguably Bastet is probably still the worst in the special snowflake department). In their own books they are all special and they are the only ones that really &quot;Get&quot; the universe. It's normal stuff. They're no less snowflaky then any of th other factions.<br /> <br /> The Ananasi do have a slightly different play style from the other shifters, but they excel at underhanded and subtle manipulations, something the other shifters usually don't deal with. They're also not the best team players, but neither are the Kitsune, Bastet, Nuwisha, Gurahl or the Corax... so...<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...Kitsune are great team players. Its why where Kitsune are there are still Multibreed septs and Packs. KItsune can and are the glue that can hold together a pack of a Nagah, Nezumi, Khan and Hakken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T03:22:28-08:00","id":792688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/792267-ananasi-too-special-snowflake?p=792680#post792680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...Kitsune are great team players. Its why where Kitsune are there are still Multibreed septs and Packs. KItsune can and are the glue that can hold together a pack of a Nagah, Nezumi, Khan and Hakken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spoken like a true kitsune fan person....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T03:48:55-08:00","id":792693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/792267-ananasi-too-special-snowflake?p=792688#post792688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spoken like a true kitsune fan person....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can quote the Shattered Dreams manuscript about them. There's a reason why the Emerald Courts are the only ones still working as Gaia Intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T08:35:40-08:00","id":792750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/792267-ananasi-too-special-snowflake?p=792693#post792693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can quote the Shattered Dreams manuscript about them. There's a reason why the Emerald Courts are the only ones still working as Gaia Intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than when some new bit of writing comes out to grimdark everything up a notch and present the Nezumi as having killed most of the Nagah in Japan, anyway. Which doesn't even make sense as far as &quot;beast rivalries&quot; goes, since the stock of the Nagah there is likely mostly made up of King Cobras, which eat other snakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T10:37:26-08:00","id":792773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/792267-ananasi-too-special-snowflake?p=792693#post792693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I can quote the Shattered Dreams manuscript about them. There's a reason why the Emerald Courts are the only ones still working as Gaia Intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're quoting a book that's still in production, and which we still don't know how it will pan out. The Kitsune came way after the Emerald courts were established, and the Hengeyokai book paints them as team players in the first part of the book, only to paint the picture with a different brush in their own breedbook - where the Kitsune simply like to mess with everything and poke their noses everywhere and the Emerald Courts are just means to an end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-25T10:38:06-08:00","id":792774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/792267-ananasi-too-special-snowflake?p=792750#post792750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other than when some new bit of writing comes out to grimdark everything up a notch and present the Nezumi as having killed most of the Nagah in Japan, anyway. Which doesn't even make sense as far as &quot;beast rivalries&quot; goes, since the stock of the Nagah there is likely mostly made up of King Cobras, which eat other snakes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, that's a thing in Shattered Dreams??!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value"